== Cited inputs (2504.02927 v2 Sect. III B, App. C)
E_i = 120 meV; YIG maximum magnon energy about 110 meV; resolution 5 meV at zero transfer; detectors to 60 deg;
q_1BZ = 987 eV; agreement with the Heisenberg-model result near 1 MeV; rapid fall below about 200 keV;
YIG sample at T < ~10 K (their App. B 2)
Fe3+ form factor: order-of-magnitude suppression for q >~ 10 keV; phonon factor (q/30 keV)^2 for m_N ~ 50 GeV, omega ~ 20 meV
Book: v_max = 794.5 km/s = 2.6502e-03

== C_sn at q -> 0 for J multiplets, [lambda_S/(g_J/2)]^2 with lambda_S = g_J - 1 (tab:14-lande, Hund's rules)
Gd3+: g_J = 2, lambda_S = 1, C_sn(0) = 1
Er3+: g_J = 6/5, lambda_S = 1/5, C_sn(0) = 1/9
Sm3+: g_J = 2/7, lambda_S = -5/7, C_sn(0) = 25

== Kinematics of the neutron probe
neutron momentum at E_i = 120 meV: p_n = 15017 eV = 15.0 keV; largest momentum transfer (backscattering) 30.0 keV
dark-matter mass whose largest momentum, m v_max, equals p_n: 5.67 MeV; its largest momentum transfer 2 m v_max = 30.0 keV
kinetic energy of that dark-matter particle at v_max: 19.9 eV (against 0.120 eV for the neutron)
mass whose largest momentum transfer 2 m v_max equals q_1BZ = 987 eV: 186 keV
bcc YIG, a = 12.56 A: 2 pi/a (Gamma to the zone corner H) = 987 eV; inscribed radius pi sqrt2/a (Gamma to N) = 698 eV; every q inside the first zone for m < (pi sqrt2/a)/(2 v_max) = 132 keV
bcc YIG, a = 12.375 A: 2 pi/a (Gamma to the zone corner H) = 1002 eV; inscribed radius pi sqrt2/a (Gamma to N) = 708 eV; every q inside the first zone for m < (pi sqrt2/a)/(2 v_max) = 134 keV
  (q_1BZ = 987 eV of 2504.02927 is 2 pi/a for their a = 12.56 A; the book's a = 12.375 A, DATA-ADDENDA)
phonon factor (q/30 keV)^2 at q = 5, 10, 15 keV: 0.028, 0.111, 0.250

